# Frontend dashboard (PRD 003)

- Next.js App Router, **TypeScript strict**. Server components by default; client components
  only for charts/live/interactivity.
- **Consume the API; never recompute metrics client-side.** Derive types from the API's
  OpenAPI contract (`openapi-typescript`) so field names match the backend/DB exactly.
- UI: Tailwind + shadcn/ui. Charts: **lightweight-charts** for price/levels/OI candles,
  **Recharts** for metric panels (PCR/sentiment/IV-skew/OI-by-strike). Data: **TanStack Query**.
- Auth via `@supabase/supabase-js` (auth only — no direct service-role DB access). Attach the
  JWT to API calls. Protected routes redirect unauthenticated users to login.
- Always handle **loading / empty (market closed) / error** states. Missing metric values
  (null `india_vix`, early `cog_shift`) render as "—", never crash.
- Live toggle subscribes to the API WebSocket; auto-reconnect with backoff, fall back to polling.
- See also the `frontend-ui` rule for UI engineering practices.
